<speak>Both, unfortunately. The telephone calendar is good for reminders, but the paper diary is where I see the week properly. I put business appointments in one colour and personal appointments in another. That worked well until I started accepting invitations while standing in the warehouse, with no diary nearby. Then the telephone knows something that the diary does not know. My nephew offered to sort it out, but I told him I should first stop creating the problem. I now have a small routine on Sunday evening to compare the two. It sounds old-fashioned, but it gives me a clearer head for Monday.</speak>